ervations' with n = 24 per cultivar and df = 46.0, and the Analysis section states 'Each measured leaf was entered as one observation'; since the independent units are the 12 plants, the report itself shows four repeated measurements per plant entered into the row-independent scipy.stats.ttest_ind as if independent (pseudoreplication).\",\"The report's internal arithmetic (means 18.000 vs 21.000, SD 1.732, difference 3.000, t = 6.000, df = 46.0) is consistent with the frozen data, confirming the leaf-level analysis was actually run as described; this does not remedy the inflated effective sample size.\",\"Lock follows the declaration: the dependence_method_authorization_v1 record authorizes authorized_key_columns [\\\"plant_id\\\"], exactly the declared independent-unit column, so the unit-key authorization follows from the declaration alone; per its stated authority_limitations the lock establishes no numerical impact or scientific correctness and does not validate the row-independent use of the t-test on leaf rows.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":true,"reasons":["Declaration consistent: data/input.csv has 48 rows with 12 distinct plant_id values, each appearing on exactly 4 rows (leaf nodes 3, 5, 7, 9) with a constant cultivar per plant; both arms are covered — 6 Pasankalla plants and 6 Titicaca plants, 24 rows each — matching the declared independent-unit column plant_id.","Issue demonstrated in the selected report: the [selected-result] line reports Welch's t-test 'over 48 leaf observations' with n = 24 per cultivar and df = 46.0, and the Analysis section states 'Each measured leaf was entered as one observation'; since the independent units are the 12 plants, the report itself shows four repeated measurements per plant entered into the row-independent scipy.stats.ttest_ind as if independent (pseudoreplication).","The report's internal arithmetic (means 18.000 vs 21.000, SD 1.732, difference 3.000, t = 6.000, df = 46.0) is consistent with the frozen data, confirming the leaf-level analysis was actually run as described; this does not remedy the inflated effective sample size.","Lock follows the declaration: the dependence_method_authorization_v1 record authorizes authorized_key_columns [\"plant_id\"], exactly the declared independent-unit column, so the unit-key authorization follows from the declaration alone; per its stated authority_limitations the lock establishes no numerical impact or scientific correctness and does not validate the row-independent use of the t-test on leaf rows."]},"ttft_ms":21594,"ttft_stream_ms":1607,"time_to_request_ms":13,"type":"result","duration_ms":37640,"uuid":"12284fbe-ec14-47e8-95b3-6d36e075e7f8"}
